\appendix

\begin{frame}
  \frametitle{Backup: Fizzle Probability}

  At the start of invasion, \(X(0)\approx1\), so one infectious lineage is
  approximately a homogeneous birth-death process with
  \[
  b=\beta,
  \qquad
  d=\gamma+\mu.
  \]

  \pause
  The extinction probability for one lineage is
  \[
  \frac{d}{b}=\frac{1}{\Rn}.
  \]

  \pause
  With \(k\) introduced infectives,
  \[
  \prob\{\text{fizzle}\}\approx \left(\frac{1}{\Rn}\right)^k,
  \qquad
  p_k=\prob\{\text{not fizzle}\}
  =
  1-\left(\frac{1}{\Rn}\right)^k.
  \]
\end{frame}

\begin{frame}
  \frametitle{Backup: The Entry Point \(\xin\)}

  The formula needs the susceptible proportion at entry into the rare
  infection layer:
  \[
  Y=\ystar=\eps\left(1-\frac{1}{\Rn}\right),
  \qquad
  X=\xin.
  \]

  \pause
  The SIAP phase-plane approximation supplies \(\xin\) analytically.

  \pause
  \[
  \xin =
  e^{-\Rn(1-\ystar)}
  + \eps e^{\Rn\ystar}
  \log\left(\frac{\ystar}{Y_{\max}}\right)
  + \Oh(\eps^2).
  \]

  % TODO: Decide later whether this belongs in the main deck or should remain
  % backup; it is background machinery rather than the main biological point.
\end{frame}

\begin{frame}
  \frametitle{Backup: Conditional Burnout Form}

  The poster and source slides also express the conditional burnout
  probability after not fizzling as
  \[
  \prob\{\text{burnout}\mid\text{not fizzle}\}
  \approx
  q^{n\ystar}.
  \]

  \pause
  Equivalently, using the Laplace approximation directly,
  \[
  \exp\left[
  -n\ystar
  \sqrt{\frac{\eps(\Rn-1)}{2\pi}}\,
  e^{-\frac{\Rn}{\eps}(\frac{1}{\Rn}-\xin)}
  \left(
  \frac{1-\xin}{1-\frac{1}{\Rn}}
  \right)^{\frac{\Rn}{\eps}(1-\frac{1}{\Rn})}
  \right].
  \]

  % TODO: Check which algebraic form David prefers for visibility.
\end{frame}

\begin{frame}
  \frametitle{Backup: Why Contours Are Expensive by Simulation}

  A single persistence probability estimate requires many stochastic
  outbreaks, each followed through the dangerous trough.

  \pause
  A contour plot repeats that calculation across hundreds or thousands of
  parameter combinations.

  \pause
  The direct approximation changes the job from repeated rare-event
  simulation to evaluating a formula.
\end{frame}

